# Security Rules

## Purpose
Protect user data, auth flows, and server-side secrets from accidental exposure.

## Scope
All frontend, backend, and config code that handles auth, tokens, or user input.

## Hard Constraints
- MUST hash passwords with bcrypt and never store plaintext credentials.
- MUST keep access tokens short-lived and refresh tokens server-side in Redis.
- MUST validate all user input at the API boundary before business logic runs.
- MUST keep secrets out of browser-exposed code and committed files.
- MUST use auth guards on protected routes.

## Best Practices
- SHOULD rotate or invalidate refresh tokens on logout and re-authentication.

## Enforceability
- Lint: secret scanning and unsafe string literal checks.
- CI: auth and input-validation tests.
- Review: reject any client-side secret access or unvalidated trust boundary.

## Examples
### ✅ Valid
```ts
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
export class ChartsController {}
```

### ❌ Invalid
```ts
const password = 'admin123';
```
